My Summer of Love is a 2004 British drama film directed by Paweł
Pawlikowski and co-written by Pawlikowski and Michael Wynne.

11
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Based on the 2001 novel of the same name by Helen Cross, the film explores the romantic
relationship between two young women from different classes and backgrounds.

12
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Working class Mona (Natalie Press), whose once-hotheaded brother Phil (Paddy Considine) became a born-again Christian in prison, meets
upper middle class Tamsin (Emily Blunt, in her theatrical film debut) who suffers from a lack of love in her family.

13
